WEBVTT

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:16.530
<i>At this rate...</i>

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:19.370
But...

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:59.510
<b>Voices of Condolence</b>

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:57.510
Look out!

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:07.870
Come on, hurry!

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:21.780
Help me...

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:23.580
<i>What?</i>

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.470
<i>This Daemonia will also...</i>

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.320
<i>I'll just let...</i>

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.040
Powers of The Magician...

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.630
Restrain!

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.280
It hurts...

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.900
Help me...

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:39.610
I leave the rest to you, Priscilla.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:40.900
Okay, Mel!

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:49.450
Attack of The Fool!

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:01.720
Do you know what you're doing?

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:06.180
Oh, no!

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:18.620
It got away. I can't believe this!

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:21.810
How do you plan to take 
responsibility for this?

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:24.070
What are you going to do if 
it causes even more harm?

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.290
You know—

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:31.950
Now, now. There's no point in 
yelling at her now.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:34.500
We'll just have to exterminate 
it for sure next time.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.320
Let's go.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.630
Am I being taken back?

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:40.940
Of course.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:43.340
Etia-san's orders are absolute.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:45.090
No.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.390
What?! After all this, 
you have the ner—

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.850
All right, then I guess 
it can't be helped.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:57.520
Try anything funny and electricity 
will run through those.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.280
How foolish.

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:07.680
The reason this organization 
exists is to protect everyone.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:09.660
Just because you leave the organization

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.620
doesn't mean you'll get 
away from the Daemonia.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.900
You'll just end up fighting alone,

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:18.570
and if you run without 
fighting, you'll only die.

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:19.600
I don't care.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:20.920
If I won't have to kill anyone—

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:24.300
So you'll die yourself. How carefree.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:29.680
By fighting the Daemonia, there 
are lives we can save, too.

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:32.580
You saved the father and son 
on the boat, did you not?

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:33.790
But...

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:35.560
I can't.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.800
This is your destiny.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:52.270
Akari is back.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:53.810
I see.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:57.130
It appears that she defended a Daemonia.

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:58.460
What are you going to do about it?

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:11.470
Um...

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:16.100
You saved me and yet... I'm sorry.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.600
Well, you've got a lot 
on your mind, right?

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:23.360
What? Akari's in the dungeon?!

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:26.610
Shh! Your voice is 
loud, Ginka Onee-tan.

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:29.340
Well of course it is 
if you tell me that.

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:30.660
What did Akari do?

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.250
She ran away from the organization. 
Of course that happened.

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:35.930
Yeah, but isn't putting 
her in a cell a bit much?

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:39.000
They said that they were going to 
let Akari Onee-tan cool off.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:39.870
They said.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.290
I wonder if she's okay.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:46.880
We will now begin the strategy meeting.

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:51.520
As previously reported,

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.680
the Daemonia infiltrate a person's soul,

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.390
using it as its host,

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:59.810
and then grow in number by multiplying.
 None of that information has changed.

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:04.900
This has not changed elsewhere 
according to the other branches.

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:08.910
Currently, the percentage 
of Daemonia possession

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:10.790
in Nagataki Ward is 0.05%.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:16.120
This doesn't include Daemonia that 
have not been completely taken over.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:20.330
It is believed that there are 
even more dormant Daemonia.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:24.710
It will take at least twenty 
weeks for the Daemonia

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.210
to possess the people of this area.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:30.650
Thinking of previous cases, we 
need to exterminate them quickly,

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:34.800
and bring the number down to 0.003%.

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:39.680
Is there no way to find 
the dormant Daemonia?

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:42.360
That's not possible, Seira Onee-tan.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:45.120
If the Daemonia don't 
enter the Astralux,

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:47.400
we can't trace their thoughts.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:51.030
Until then, the thoughts of the human 
it's possessing get in the way

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:52.660
so we can't find them.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:53.450
Find them!

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:56.200
What the heck? That 
means we're too late.

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:59.830
The purpose of our organization 
is extermination.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:01.890
If nothing happens, we don't act.

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:03.210
Right.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:06.210
I want to exterminate 
them more efficiently.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.800
I don't want innocent people to die.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.720
The Daemonia are no longer human.

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:17.720
To protect humanity, we 
must stop the infection.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:21.730
Please do not feel 
guilt for the extermination.

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:25.230
We are just following our destiny.

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:26.380
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.490
Destiny...

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:39.990
<i>What was my mom feeling when...</i>

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:42.750
<i>How did she feel...</i>

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:49.250
<i>Help me...</i>

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.260
<i>It hurts...</i>

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:53.800
<i>Help me...</i>

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:08.020
<i>Was that the Daemonia's voice I heard?</i>

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:11.030
<i>So what if it was?</i>

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:13.530
<i>I can't even save anyone.</i>

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:16.990
<i>No one...</i>

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:32.140
I wonder what Akari's going to do.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:33.370
I wonder if she's going to quit.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:36.090
Even if she does, nothing will change.

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:37.630
We'll just fight with the three of us.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:41.390
I'd like her to stay.

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:44.170
We don't need any indecisive people.

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:45.640
We're risking our lives.

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:51.970
I wouldn't say that 
I'm risking my life,

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:53.570
but I'm in it for the reward.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.790
I guess you could call me indecisive.

00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:58.660
Where are you going?

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:01.280
I'm going to bring Akari-san some food.

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:07.260
She sure is assertive 
when it comes to Akari.

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:08.250
You think so?

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:20.760
I thought you might be hungry,

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.430
so I got permission from Etia-san.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:24.440
Oh...

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:37.430
You need to eat something.

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:50.320
I was put into this cell, too.

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:54.170
Three months ago, when 
I first came here.

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:56.820
I couldn't fight a Daemonia.

00:10:58.010 --> 00:11:01.970
Seira-san and Ginka-san had 
been here for six months,

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:04.000
so they worked perfectly together.

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:06.310
But I was too scared.

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:07.180
Luna-chan...

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:10.900
It's true that because of the Daemonia, 
innocent people will be killed

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:12.310
and there will be unfortunate events.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:16.150
There may be no other 
way than to exterminate them.

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:19.850
But...

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:22.920
Everyone forgets about the people

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:24.450
who have turned into Daemonia,

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:28.200
even though they lived in this world.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:32.310
That's so sad and scary.

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:38.210
I heard them...

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:38.960
Huh?

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:40.470
The Daemonia's voices.

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:42.570
When I was fighting them.

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:44.470
What do you mean?

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:46.950
I don't know.

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:48.740
I don't even know why I heard it.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:02.790
There!

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:14.420
Hey.

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:17.170
You should be heading home now.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:18.860
Okay!

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:28.450
197, 198, 199, 200...

00:12:36.390 --> 00:12:38.440
Everything's fine.

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:43.790
We're fighting for justice, 
and it pays pretty well.

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:48.980
You don't need to worry, Pops.

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:08.350
This one is the next 
one to awaken, right?

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:12.280
Even though it's for humanity, in 
the end, they're just killers.

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:13.670
What to do.

00:13:13.670 --> 00:13:15.420
We can just use her to

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:17.180
protect the interests of 
the Tsukuyomi Conglomerate.

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:18.360
Send her out as a hostage.

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:22.540
She's already damaged goods 
anyway, so it's perfect for her.

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:31.770
It's okay.

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:35.700
You're not damaged goods, Luna.

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:43.850
Serena Onee-chan!

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:45.580
Onee-chan!

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:47.130
Over here.

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.400
<i>Everyone forgets about the people</i>

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:07.030
<i>who have turned into Daemonia,</i>

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:10.870
<i>even though they lived in this world.</i>

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:29.260
<i>I won't forget. Never again.</i>

00:14:35.590 --> 00:14:37.350
What did you want to talk about?

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:39.600
I heard it.

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:42.050
I heard the voice of the person 
who turned into a Daemonia.

00:14:42.050 --> 00:14:42.860
What?

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:45.320
It kept saying "help 
me" over and over.

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:46.970
That is not possible.

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:49.050
The Daemonia move by taking over

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:51.620
a person's body as well as their mind.

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.410
There's no way they can talk.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:57.170
They're not human 
anymore, just puppets.

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:58.110
Puppets!

00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:59.960
But I know I heard...

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:02.000
The Daemonia aren't human.

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:04.480
Stop feeling sorry for them.

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:06.390
Feeling sorry for them won't change

00:15:06.390 --> 00:15:09.100
the fact that they need 
to be exterminated.

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:11.010
That might be true, but...

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:12.130
But what?

00:15:12.130 --> 00:15:14.010
Are you trying to say 
there's a way to save them?

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:19.910
I'm not sure yet,

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:23.520
but I will find the answer myself.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:26.780
So, I will participate in the battle.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:39.540
<i>I can come back?</i>

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:44.170
<i>Yes. If you're going 
to fight, that is fine.</i>

00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:48.050
Akari-san!

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:49.880
What happened to you?

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:52.270
W-Well, a lot happened.

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:53.300
If...

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.810
...you can't fight again, 
I won't hold back.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:04.100
She heard their voices.

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:05.730
Is that even possible?

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:07.020
I'm not sure.

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:09.570
But I don't think it's impossible.

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:20.370
The choo-choo train goes 
into the mountains.

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:24.880
Choo-choo, choo-choo, 
puffing black smoke.

00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:26.630
Chugga-chugga, chugga-chugga...

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:29.750
You're coming back?

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:31.230
Yes.

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:32.260
I see.

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:36.220
I'm still not sure what I should do.

00:16:36.240 --> 00:16:40.140
It's not like I can save them 
just because I can hear them.

00:16:41.090 --> 00:16:42.140
But...

00:16:42.630 --> 00:16:46.100
I can't run away without 
doing anything either.

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:50.820
I think I can, I think I can,

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:52.990
I think I can, I think I can.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:55.320
Tunnel, iron bridge, 
choo-choo, choo-choo.

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:57.660
Tunnel, iron bridge, 
chugga-chugga, chugga-chugga.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:00.400
Tunnel, iron bridge, 
tunnel, iron bridge...

00:17:19.150 --> 00:17:21.310
It's all right. It's all right.

00:17:33.270 --> 00:17:37.030
Bring it on! One million dollars in gold coins!

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:47.250
Protect them!

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:02.260
Help me, please...

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:04.640
Help me...

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:08.490
I can hear your voice.

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:15.920
I can hear you.

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:17.240
What are you going to do?

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:19.820
I'm going to listen,

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:21.580
because that's what it wants.

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:27.160
If you're going to get in 
the way, I won't hold back.

00:18:30.350 --> 00:18:31.170
Move!

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:39.430
What are you...

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:42.890
I believe. I believe 
what Akari-san says.

00:18:51.410 --> 00:18:52.580
Luna-chan...

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:07.040
It hurts. I'm lonely.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:08.460
Why?

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:10.790
What do you want to tell me?

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:21.550
Why did he...

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:33.310
I was told if I kill children, 
he would be brought back to life.

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:37.230
But, he didn't come back.

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:43.700
I don't want to hurt 
any more children.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:51.460
Stop messing around!

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:54.710
I'm sorry, I'm at my limit!

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:12.900
Sensei!

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:15.560
Kill me...

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:19.030
You do it.

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:21.890
Please...

00:20:28.570 --> 00:20:30.030
This is the en—

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:03.650
This is my...

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:06.280
...destiny.

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:15.170
So you've found it.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:17.340
Your own answer.

00:21:17.840 --> 00:21:20.420
I believe that I have no other 
choice but to bear this.

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:23.920
I will never be forgiven for 
what happened to Fuyuna.

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:30.930
But if I don't accept it, her 
death will only be in vain.

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:33.980
I want to be able to remember

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:37.100
what the people who 
turned into Daemonia

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:38.560
were feeling.

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:41.190
I see.

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:46.450
But that will be very 
difficult for you.

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:52.540
But, follow the path 
you believe is right.

00:22:02.380 --> 00:22:06.630
The Daemonia's voices, 
huh? Very interesting.

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:08.720
Let's let her swim for a while.

00:22:08.980 --> 00:22:11.560
Indeed. She's a wonderful guinea pig.

00:22:11.560 --> 00:22:13.920
Let us wait a little 
longer on the report.

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:41.510
<b>#15     The Devil</b>

00:23:27.040 --> 00:23:28.790
We're the Tendo Sisters!

00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:33.280
This week's card is The Devil.

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:32.740
<b>The Devil card defines people's
 greed, jealousy and hatred.</b>

00:23:32.740 --> 00:23:34.910
<b>The card cautions that these wicked
 feelings have taken over and you are 
not longer able to think straight.</b>

00:23:33.280 --> 00:23:35.170
Itsuki-chan's tone is the devil.

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:36.970
<b>If you choose this card, you will
 be filled with doubts and jealousy,
 you will become pessimistic and 
everything will seem hopeless.</b>

00:23:35.170 --> 00:23:36.390
The devil!

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:38.770
<b>You will feel like doing nothing. 
That is what this card shows.</b>

00:23:37.930 --> 00:23:41.390
<b>Is This a Painting?</b>

00:23:38.560 --> 00:23:40.980
See you next time!

00:23:38.770 --> 00:23:41.410
<b>However, if the card is reversed, 
and you throw away all of your 
obsessions and concerns, you will be 
relieved from your suffering and see
 the end of your predicament. 
It shows that your luck might be improving.</b>
